---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config.js';
import { Archive, BadgeCheck, ChevronRight, CircleCheck, CodeXml, Compass, GitFork, RefreshCw, Rocket, Scale, Star, TriangleAlert, Unplug } from '@lucide/astro';

const title = `Our Methodology | ${SITE_NAME}`;
const description = 'The public methodology behind X-fit, tool status, last-checked dates, API labels, testing and editorial recommendations.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <main class="about-page">
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="about-hero-inner">
        <nav class="breadcrumbs about-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a><ChevronRight size={15} stroke-width={1.8} aria-hidden="true" />
          <span aria-current="page">Methodology</span>
        </nav>
        <div class="about-hero-content">
          <div class="about-hero-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Scale size={36} stroke-width={1.7} /></div>
          <div>
            <h1>Facts first, with a date</h1>
            <p>Our labels answer a practical question: does this product still do a meaningful job on X today? Here is exactly how we decide.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="about-body methodology-body">
      <section class="about-overview">
        <p>We do not rank tools with an invented popularity number. We record observable product facts, make the editorial judgment behind X-fit explicit, and show when each listing was last checked.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="x-fit-title">
        <div class="about-section-heading"><span>01 · X-fit</span><h2 id="x-fit-title">How central is X to the product?</h2></div>
        <div class="about-method-grid methodology-fit-grid">
          <article class="about-method-card methodology-fit-card">
            <div class="methodology-fit-label fit-high"><span class="x-fit-meter" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><h3>High</h3></div>
            <p>X is the product or its core job: threads, replies, bookmarks, X analytics, account hygiene, or direct X API workflows.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="about-method-card methodology-fit-card">
            <div class="methodology-fit-label fit-medium"><span class="x-fit-meter" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><h3>Medium</h3></div>
            <p>The product supports several networks, but X remains first-class with a real composer, analytics, listening, or publishing workflow.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="about-method-card methodology-fit-card">
            <div class="methodology-fit-label fit-low"><span class="x-fit-meter" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><h3>Low</h3></div>
            <p>X is incidental, lightly supported, or mainly a distribution checkbox for a product built around another job or network.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="status-title">
        <div class="about-section-heading"><span>02 · Freshness</span><h2 id="status-title">Operational status is separate from visibility</h2><p>We retain useful historical pages so an old recommendation does not silently become a broken link.</p></div>
        <div class="methodology-definition-list">
          <div><strong><span class="tool-status-chip status-live"><CircleCheck size={12} stroke-width={2} aria-hidden="true" />Live</span></strong><span>The product is operating and any X workflow described in its listing is currently available. Adjacent tools can be live without being X-native.</span></div>
          <div><strong><span class="tool-status-chip status-degraded"><TriangleAlert size={12} stroke-width={2} aria-hidden="true" />Degraded</span></strong><span>The tool works, but an important X feature is limited, unreliable, or materially changed.</span></div>
          <div><strong><span class="tool-status-chip status-dropped-x"><Unplug size={12} stroke-width={2} aria-hidden="true" />Dropped X</span></strong><span>The product remains active but no longer supports its former X workflow.</span></div>
          <div><strong><span class="tool-status-chip status-shut-down"><Archive size={12} stroke-width={2} aria-hidden="true" />Shut down</span></strong><span>The product is no longer operating. Its page remains as a clearly marked historical reference.</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="api-title">
        <div class="about-section-heading"><span>03 · API honesty</span><h2 id="api-title">A green badge requires verification</h2></div>
        <div class="about-method-grid">
          <article class="about-method-card"><span class="about-method-icon"><CodeXml size={21} /></span><h3>Official API</h3><p>The main X job publishes or reads through X's official API. API classifications appear in tool overviews. Card API badges are currently paused pending a consistent verification pass.</p></article>
          <article class="about-method-card"><span class="about-method-icon"><CodeXml size={21} /></span><h3>Official API + other data</h3><p>At least part of the workflow uses the official API, while extensions, scraping, imported data, or other sources are also involved.</p></article>
          <article class="about-method-card"><span class="about-method-icon"><CodeXml size={21} /></span><h3>No API or unclear</h3><p>Extensions and local tools can still be excellent. When we cannot verify the access method, we say so rather than awarding a badge.</p></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="badges-title">
        <div class="about-section-heading"><span>04 · Editorial labels</span><h2 id="badges-title">What the other badges mean</h2></div>
        <div class="methodology-definition-list methodology-badge-list">
          <div><strong><span class="verified-date-chip"><BadgeCheck size={14} stroke-width={2} aria-hidden="true" />Last checked</span></strong><span>The date at the bottom right of each tool card records our latest review of its listing. It is not a guarantee of current availability or a claim of hands-on testing.</span></div>
          <div><strong><span class="badge-editor-pick"><Star size={12} stroke-width={2.2} fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" /> Editor's Pick</span></strong><span>A Live, High-X-fit tool we would put on a serious shortlist for its job.</span></div>
          <div><strong><span class="badge-x-native">X-native</span></strong><span>A product whose only listed network is X, with Live or Degraded status. “Built just for X” describes the same network scope regardless of status. High X-fit is a separate assessment and can apply to multi-network tools.</span></div>
          <div><strong><span class="badge-founder-built"><Rocket size={12} stroke-width={1.8} fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" /> Founder-built</span></strong><span>The original maker or a small founding team still operates the product.</span></div>
          <div><strong><span class="badge-open-source"><GitFork size={12} stroke-width={2.2} aria-hidden="true" /> Open source</span></strong><span>The product publishes its source code under an open-source license. A public repository alone does not imply that the hosted service is free.</span></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="sources-title">
        <div class="about-section-heading"><span>05 · Discovery</span><h2 id="sources-title">Where new tools come from</h2></div>
        <div class="methodology-source-note">
          <span class="methodology-source-icon" aria-hidden="true"><Compass size={21} stroke-width={1.9} /></span>
          <p>We review maker launch posts, product documentation, open-source repositories and the official <a href="https://developer.x.com/exhibit" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X Developer Exhibit</a>. Discovery is not verification: every candidate still needs a working first-party product page and enough evidence to describe its current X workflow accurately.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-submit-cta">
        <div><p class="about-submit-eyebrow">Corrections stay open</p><h2>Product facts change</h2><p>A last checked date records our latest review, not a permanent guarantee. Makers and readers can submit corrections; we verify them before publishing.</p></div>
        <a class="hero-action hero-action-primary" href="/submit/">Suggest an update<RefreshCw size={16} /></a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
